export default [{"s":1.12,"e":2.8,"t":"Episode 1."},{"s":2.94,"e":6.36,"t":"Where to start reading X-Men without losing your mind."},{"s":7.3,"e":11.91,"t":"A few years ago I walked into Graham Crackers Comics in Chicago as a grown adult and"},{"s":11.96,"e":15.15,"t":"asked the guy behind the counter the most embarrassing question you can ask in a"},{"s":15.2,"e":16.32,"t":"comic shop."},{"s":16.7,"e":18.64,"t":"Where do I start with X-Men?"},{"s":19.12,"e":24.19,"t":"Because X-Men is 60 years of comics, a dozen books with X-Men in the title and"},{"s":24.24,"e":27.34,"t":"reading orders online that look like tax forms."},{"s":27.72,"e":31.24,"t":"He didn't hand me a reading order, he handed me one book."},{"s":31.32,"e":32.4,"t":"And it worked."},{"s":33.4,"e":35.44,"t":"So that's what this video is."},{"s":35.52,"e":36.79,"t":"Not a reading order."},{"s":36.84,"e":38.65,"t":"Five books. One shelf."},{"s":38.7,"e":39.72,"t":"Let's go."},{"s":40.64,"e":41.76,"t":"Quick background."},{"s":42.4,"e":46.85,"t":"I was eight years old growing up in Chicagoland in 1992 when X-Men the animated"},{"s":46.9,"e":50.2,"t":"series came on and flipped a switch in my brain."},{"s":50.4,"e":55.86,"t":"That theme song still lives rent free and it gets me pumped every single time."},{"s":56.1,"e":58.51,"t":"My best friend is the one who got us all into it."},{"s":58.56,"e":60.95,"t":"The cartoon, the comics, all of it."},{"s":61,"e":64.7,"t":"So he got first pick and he picked Gambit, obviously."},{"s":65.14,"e":67.82,"t":"Gambit and Wolverine were the coolest guys on the show."},{"s":67.92,"e":71.79,"t":"And Gambit had the trench coat, glowing cards and accent none of us could"},{"s":71.84,"e":73,"t":"understand."},{"s":73.26,"e":77.6,"t":"He also decided the girl everybody in class had a crush on was Rogue."},{"s":77.8,"e":78.6,"t":"Kids."},{"s":80.24,"e":81.64,"t":"I got Colossus."},{"s":82.12,"e":83.52,"t":"And I felt cheated."},{"s":83.74,"e":89.51,"t":"Big Russian guy turns into steel says about four words an episode but he was mine so"},{"s":89.56,"e":90.9,"t":"I stuck with him."},{"s":91.06,"e":94.56,"t":"And somewhere along the way I actually started to care about him."},{"s":94.82,"e":96.93,"t":"Strongest guy in the room and he'd rather be home painting."},{"s":96.98,"e":100.53,"t":"I don't think I'm the only one this happened to."},{"s":100.58,"e":102.71,"t":"A lot of us didn't pick our X-Man."},{"s":102.76,"e":105.66,"t":"We got handed one and then we got attached."},{"s":106.09,"e":108.15,"t":"That's how I got into X-Men."},{"s":108.21,"e":111.01,"t":"Not through a reading order, through a character."},{"s":111.29,"e":112.38,"t":"Hold on to that."},{"s":112.43,"e":114.58,"t":"I'm going to come back to it in a minute."},{"s":114.63,"e":117.63,"t":"The obvious move is to start at the beginning."},{"s":117.75,"e":119.18,"t":"X-Men number one."},{"s":119.23,"e":120.09,"t":"1963."},{"s":121.01,"e":122.63,"t":"It matters historically."},{"s":122.79,"e":124.26,"t":"Stan Lee and Jack Kirby."},{"s":124.31,"e":125.73,"t":"The original five."},{"s":126.09,"e":127.75,"t":"Magneto's first appearance."},{"s":127.91,"e":130.13,"t":"Honestly, it feels like a different team."},{"s":130.33,"e":134.1,"t":"But it's good background and it matters more than you'd think once we get to"},{"s":134.15,"e":135.07,"t":"Hickman."},{"s":135.39,"e":137.13,"t":"Hold that thought, too."},{"s":137.49,"e":141.76,"t":"But historically important and a good first read are not the same thing."},{"s":141.81,"e":145.74,"t":"The storytelling has changed a lot in 60 years. And you don't need to do homework to"},{"s":145.79,"e":147.25,"t":"enjoy this stuff."},{"s":147.79,"e":149.86,"t":"So treat it like a tasting menu."},{"s":149.91,"e":151.93,"t":"Five stories from different eras."},{"s":152.05,"e":154.04,"t":"If one grabs you, follow it."},{"s":154.09,"e":156.12,"t":"If one doesn't, skip it."},{"s":156.17,"e":157.35,"t":"Nobody's checking."},{"s":157.89,"e":159.43,"t":"Number one."},{"s":159.53,"e":161.08,"t":"The Dark Phoenix saga."},{"s":161.13,"e":164.21,"t":"Uncanny X-Men 129 through 137."},{"s":164.41,"e":167.29,"t":"1980. Chris Claremont and John Byrne."},{"s":167.63,"e":171.27,"t":"If you only read one X-Men story, it's probably this one."},{"s":171.51,"e":173.58,"t":"It's the team at their peak."},{"s":173.63,"e":177.17,"t":"And it's where a lot of what you know about the X-Men comes from."},{"s":177.28,"e":181.27,"t":"Issue 129 alone introduces Kitty Pryde and Emma Frost."},{"s":181.63,"e":187.61,"t":"130 gives you Dazzler, who's a disco superhero and it's not as corny as it sounds."},{"s":187.81,"e":189.99,"t":"But the real story is Jean Grey."},{"s":190.27,"e":192.83,"t":"She's gained cosmic power."},{"s":192.99,"e":196.19,"t":"The Hellfire Club is introduced and messes with her head."},{"s":196.33,"e":198.65,"t":"And it goes about as well as you'd expect."},{"s":198.83,"e":203.32,"t":"What makes it hold up is that it's not just a big fight like Secret Wars."},{"s":203.37,"e":206.55,"t":"It's a team trying to save a friend from herself."},{"s":207.17,"e":208.43,"t":"And then 137."},{"s":208.77,"e":210.74,"t":"I'm not going to spoil it for you."},{"s":210.79,"e":214.67,"t":"I'll just say it's one of the most famous endings in comics for a reason."},{"s":214.85,"e":218.76,"t":"I've been through the Phoenix story a bunch of times before I ever read the actual"},{"s":218.81,"e":219.75,"t":"book."},{"s":219.81,"e":222.91,"t":"The cartoon did it and honestly did it really well."},{"s":222.99,"e":227.1,"t":"The movies have tried it twice and I'm still waiting for one to get it right."},{"s":227.15,"e":228.54,"t":"But it didn't matter."},{"s":228.59,"e":232.62,"t":"Even knowing how it ends, the trade paperback is still the best way to experience"},{"s":232.67,"e":233.81,"t":"it."},{"s":234.13,"e":238.98,"t":"Team dynamics, real consequences, and a character arc that people are still adapting"},{"s":239.03,"e":240.63,"t":"40 years later."},{"s":240.95,"e":244.22,"t":"If you start anywhere, start here."},{"s":244.27,"e":245.29,"t":"Number 2."},{"s":245.69,"e":247.05,"t":"Days of Future Past."},{"s":247.39,"e":250.37,"t":"Uncanny X-Men 141 and 142."},{"s":250.67,"e":251.84,"t":"Short and sweet."},{"s":251.89,"e":252.97,"t":"Two issues."},{"s":253.69,"e":255.4,"t":"That covers the whole pitch."},{"s":255.45,"e":259.61,"t":"A future where Sentinels won and most of the X-Men are dead or in camps."},{"s":260.17,"e":263.87,"t":"Kitty's mind gets sent back to the present to stop it from happening."},{"s":264.01,"e":268.14,"t":"It's short, it's dark, and it's the blueprint for every stop the bad future story"},{"s":268.19,"e":270.14,"t":"the X-Men have done since."},{"s":270.19,"e":273.61,"t":"Including the movie and the cartoon episode you probably saw first."},{"s":273.93,"e":275.57,"t":"Number 3."},{"s":275.97,"e":277.17,"t":"X-Cutioner's Song."},{"s":277.51,"e":280.03,"t":"This one's for the kids who grew up on the cartoon."},{"s":280.41,"e":284.63,"t":"'92 into '93. A crossover across four X-books."},{"s":284.97,"e":289.88,"t":"Professor X gets shot, Cable's the main suspect, and it turns into a whole mess with"},{"s":289.93,"e":290.92,"t":"Stryfe and Apocalypse."},{"s":290.97,"e":294.82,"t":"It is the most 90s thing you will ever read."},{"s":294.87,"e":298.49,"t":"Everybody's squinting, everybody has pouches, it's pretty rad."},{"s":298.79,"e":302.68,"t":"If the cartoon is your X-Men, this is the comic that feels like it."},{"s":302.73,"e":304.72,"t":"Fair warning, it is messy."},{"s":304.77,"e":308.23,"t":"It jumps across four different books, so grab the trade paperback."},{"s":308.33,"e":310.53,"t":"Puts everything in order for you."},{"s":310.67,"e":312.25,"t":"Number 4."},{"s":312.33,"e":314.03,"t":"God Loves Man Kills."},{"s":314.17,"e":315.37,"t":"1982."},{"s":316.09,"e":318.79,"t":"Chris Claremont and Brent Anderson."},{"s":319.07,"e":320.97,"t":"A standalone graphic novel."},{"s":321.69,"e":323.44,"t":"No continuity homework."},{"s":323.49,"e":325.65,"t":"You pick it up, you read it, you're done."},{"s":325.95,"e":330.4,"t":"A preacher named William Stryker starts a crusade against mutants and the X-Men end"},{"s":330.45,"e":332.89,"t":"up working with Magneto to stop him."},{"s":333.09,"e":337.17,"t":"This is the X-Men that they're most direct about what they've always been about."},{"s":337.41,"e":340.85,"t":"Fear, prejudice, people being hated for what they are."},{"s":341.19,"e":345.05,"t":"It's also the backbone of the second X-Men movie if that's your entry point."},{"s":345.31,"e":348.89,"t":"It's heavy, but it's the one that shows you why these stories still matter."},{"s":349.17,"e":350.86,"t":"Number 5."},{"s":350.91,"e":351.99,"t":"House of M."},{"s":352.13,"e":357.49,"t":"2005. The legendary Brian Michael Bendis and Olivier Coipel."},{"s":358.17,"e":361.55,"t":"This is the book the guy at Graham Crackers handed me."},{"s":361.91,"e":367.2,"t":"The Scarlet Witch rewrites reality."},{"s":367.25,"e":370.92,"t":"Everybody wakes up in a world where they got what they wanted and a few of them"},{"s":370.97,"e":373.09,"t":"start to realize something's wrong."},{"s":373.97,"e":378.53,"t":"It's an event book, so it's big and loud and it touches the Avengers too."},{"s":378.75,"e":383.15,"t":"But it reads clean and it was the perfect way back in for me as a young adult."},{"s":384.13,"e":387.13,"t":"And the ending changed the X-Men for about a decade."},{"s":387.69,"e":390.59,"t":"Three words. You'll know them when you see them."},{"s":391.45,"e":395.12,"t":"Once you've got a few of these under your belt, then read House of X and Powers of"},{"s":395.17,"e":396.86,"t":"X. 2019,"},{"s":396.91,"e":398.23,"t":"Jonathan Hickman."},{"s":398.31,"e":405.36,"t":"It's 12 issues that flip decades of X-Men history on its head."},{"s":405.41,"e":407.16,"t":"Remember X-Men number 1?"},{"s":407.21,"e":410.4,"t":"This is where Xavier's choices, going all the way back to the beginning,"},{"s":410.45,"e":412.13,"t":"start catching up with him."},{"s":412.31,"e":413.18,"t":"It's brilliant."},{"s":413.23,"e":414.1,"t":"And it's also a lot."},{"s":414.15,"e":417.86,"t":"It lands so much harder when you know who these people are and what they've been"},{"s":417.91,"e":419.46,"t":"through. So don't start there."},{"s":419.51,"e":421.83,"t":"Save it. It'll be waiting."},{"s":422.57,"e":424.47,"t":"And here's my actual advice."},{"s":424.75,"e":425.84,"t":"Shop like a kid."},{"s":425.89,"e":429.18,"t":"When you were 10, you didn't need a reading order."},{"s":429.23,"e":433.53,"t":"You grabbed whatever cover looked cool and figured it out."},{"s":433.82,"e":435.65,"t":"Find a character you like."},{"s":435.7,"e":438.67,"t":"For me it was Colossus and I didn't even pick him."},{"s":438.72,"e":440.38,"t":"For you it might be Storm."},{"s":440.66,"e":442.32,"t":"Then you can follow them."},{"s":442.48,"e":447.06,"t":"Read their stories, jump around, get confused, look stuff up."},{"s":447.18,"e":448.54,"t":"That's half the fun."},{"s":449.36,"e":450.7,"t":"Quick note."},{"s":450.94,"e":454.63,"t":"I built ComixCatalog because I wanted one place to track what I own and what I'm"},{"s":454.68,"e":455.56,"t":"hunting."},{"s":455.64,"e":459.13,"t":"You can search any of these books, see the covers, and throw the ones you want on a"},{"s":459.18,"e":463.62,"t":"wantlist so you're not standing in a shop trying to remember issue numbers."},{"s":463.82,"e":465.35,"t":"It's free to use."},{"s":465.4,"e":466.56,"t":"Link's below."},{"s":466.68,"e":468.22,"t":"So the shelf."},{"s":468.64,"e":469.55,"t":"Dark Phoenix,"},{"s":469.6,"e":471.07,"t":"Days of Future Past,"},{"s":471.12,"e":474.35,"t":"X-Cutioner's Song, God Loves Man Kills,"},{"s":474.4,"e":475.6,"t":"and House of M."},{"s":475.88,"e":478.76,"t":"And then House of X and Powers of X when you're ready."},{"s":479.22,"e":481.86,"t":"Don't turn reading comics into homework."},{"s":482,"e":485.56,"t":"Go pick up a comic and come back and tell me which one you started with."}];
